.TH BYTEKEYS 1 "October 2026" "ByteKeys 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bytekeys \- control laptop keyboard lighting, fans and performance modes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bytekeys
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-local\fR] [\fB\-\-demo\fR]
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B bytekeys-gui
[\fB\-\-minimized\fR] [\fB\-\-demo\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ByteKeys
controls the keyboard lighting of Linux laptops (single-color backlights and
single-zone, multi-zone or per-key RGB keyboards), their performance modes,
firmware fan curves and battery charge limit. It talks to the
.B bytekeysd
system service when it is running and otherwise drives the hardware directly
("portable mode", limited to what the current user may change).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show detected keyboards and their lighting (the default command).
.TP
.B list
List device identifiers.
.TP
.BR on " | " off " | " toggle
Switch the lights.
.TP
.BI brightness " VALUE"
Set brightness in percent, or
.BR up / down
by one step.
.TP
.BI color " COLOR " "[COLOR...]"
Set the color as #rrggbb, r,g,b or a name. Several colors set one zone each;
.BI \-\-zone " N"
changes a single zone.
.TP
.BI effect " NAME"
Play an effect.
.BR \-\-speed ,
.B \-\-direction
and repeated
.B \-\-color
tune it. See
.BR effects .
.TP
.B effects
List the effects each keyboard supports.
.TP
.BR profile " list | save | apply | delete | rename"
Manage lighting profiles.
.TP
.BR rules " [list | enable ID | disable ID | export | import FILE]"
Manage automation rules.
.TP
.BR feature " [NAME [VALUE]]"
Show or change device specific settings such as firmware timeouts.
.TP
.B flash
Blink the keyboard
.RB ( \-\-color ,
.BR \-\-count ,
.BR \-\-period ),
e.g. from a notification script.
.TP
.BR perf " [MODE]"
Show the performance modes the firmware offers, or switch to
.I MODE
(for example
.BR quiet ,
.B balanced
or
.BR performance ).
.TP
.BR fans " [boost on|off | custom FAN | firmware FAN | reset FAN]"
Show temperatures, fan speeds and fan curves. Switch full fan speed on or off,
turn a fan's saved custom curve on
.RB ( custom )
or hand the fan back to the firmware's curve
.RB ( firmware ),
or forget the custom curve
.RB ( reset ).
Curves are edited in the control center; FAN 1 is the CPU fan, 2 the GPU fan.
.TP
.BR charge-limit " [PERCENT]"
Show or set the battery charge limit.
.TP
.B sensors
Show the readings automation rules use.
.TP
.B report
Print a diagnostic report for bug reports.
.TP
.B rescan
Look for keyboards again.
.TP
.BR service " install | uninstall | status"
Install or remove the system service (for source checkouts and the AppImage).
.TP
.B gui
Open the control center.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-d " DEVICE" "\fR, \fP\-\-device " DEVICE
Act on one device (default: all).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine readable output.
.TP
.B \-\-local
Do not use the service.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Add simulated keyboards and fans.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/bytekeys/state.json
Lighting, rules, profiles, fan curves and settings stored by the service.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/bytekeys/state.json
The same, in portable mode.
.TP
.I /run/bytekeys/bytekeysd.sock
Control socket of the service.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bytekeys brightness 60
bytekeys color "#ff8800"
bytekeys effect wave \-\-speed 70
bytekeys profile apply Night
bytekeys flash \-\-color red \-\-count 3
bytekeys perf performance
bytekeys fans boost on
bytekeys charge\-limit 80
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR openrgb (1)
.SH BUGS
Please report problems, with the output of
.BR "bytekeys report" ,
at https://github.com/isthatdhruv/ByteKeys/issues
